# Encoding fixtures must survive checkout BYTE-FOR-BYTE.
#
# design/reproducers/TRDD-BKALIK1B/ holds deliberately non-UTF-8 Python files
# (UTF-16 with and without a BOM). Git's text handling would treat them as text
# and normalise line endings on a checkout with core.autocrlf=true — which
# rewrites bytes inside what is really wide-encoded content and can turn the
# fixture into something a UTF-8 decoder accepts.
#
# That failure is silent and it is worse than losing the fixture: the regression
# test would still run and still pass, because the file it now reads is no
# longer a reproducer. Marking the directory binary disables every content
# filter, so the bytes that land on disk are the bytes that were committed.
design/reproducers/** -text -diff
